# F1a: the in-place slide at 2 KV heads, WATCHER pass (NoC sanitiser, waypoints, the quick matrix, no timing, a per-call watchdog).
# One card, the served draft K/V slide kernel at TWO KV heads per chip (the four-card bank (1, 2, 2048, 128), delta (1, 2, 32, 128), 8 workers
# per bank): in place (io [bank, delta, bank]) against out of place and the eager chain, byte for byte, the 1 x 80 layout of one user's ten
# banks (one program, 80 workers), and the ramp cases (drop 0). This is the one-card proof the in-place fused commit rests on; the harness runs
# its own pinned image and mounts this checkout's scripts, so it does not use the F0 image. It needs a SEPARATE tag: cardm cannot run while
# the four cards are held by a quad step.
# Duration (estimate): 10-25 min (container timeout 15 min; a hang trips the watchdog, exit 3, then reset the target card only).
# Read: the verdict passed=true for both kernels (served direct 1679bbd7 and scalar bc45d472), forms: aliased exact, every case equal, and no watcher error or assert line. STOP on any inexact byte, a watcher error, a hang.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card fused-commit window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fcommit and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (the tag numbers are
# the driver's, on the allowlist). Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image F0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fcommit-1 is a PLACEHOLDER: set it (in every template of the window) to the tag the driver picks.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fcommit-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/draft_slide_inplace/run_card_b.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--heads 2
C2_CARDM_ENV=WATCHER=1
